# Domain Layer Purity

The domain layer is the innermost layer and **must remain framework-agnostic**. Reference entity: [apps/booking-service/src/domain/entities/booking.entity.ts](../../apps/booking-service/src/domain/entities/booking.entity.ts). Reference use case: [apps/booking-service/src/domain/use-cases/create-booking.use-case.ts](../../apps/booking-service/src/domain/use-cases/create-booking.use-case.ts).

## Hard Bans Inside `domain/`

- **Never** import from `@nestjs/*`. No decorators, no DI tokens, no Nest types.
- **Never** import from `infrastructure/`, `entrypoints/`, `config/`, or `app.ts`.
- **Never** import ORM libraries (Prisma, TypeORM, Drizzle, etc.) or any I/O client.
- **Never** call `console.*`, `fetch`, `process.env`, or filesystem APIs.

## Entities (`domain/entities/`)

- Define pure TypeScript classes.
- Store state in a single `private readonly props` field typed by a `<Name>Props` interface.
- Expose state through public getters; never expose `props` directly.
- Mark interface fields `readonly`.
- Domain errors must extend `DomainError` from `@ente-doctor/common` and carry a `code: string`.

## Use Cases (`domain/use-cases/`)

- One use case per file. File name in `kebab-case.use-case.ts`, class in `PascalCase` ending in `UseCase`.
- Define a `<Name>Command` interface above the class; the `execute` method must accept that command.
- `execute` returns `Promise<void>` or a typed result. Never `any`.
- Repositories and adapters are injected through the constructor **as interface types**, never as concrete classes. Define those interfaces here (or alongside the entity) and let `infrastructure/` implement them.
- **Never** instantiate repositories or adapters inside a use case.

## Shared Package Use

- Allowed: `@ente-doctor/common` (`Logger`, `DomainError`) and `@ente-doctor/contracts` (refs, DTOs, localization).
- Forbidden: `@ente-doctor/event-bus` here. Topic publishing belongs at the entrypoints or infrastructure layer.
